			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844881">
									

<p>I understand that new authors typically don't write Keter-class scips, but this one just stuck with me, so here I am.</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Mystery, Horror, Action with hints of desperation</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Standard format (no ACS)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A solar system that is roughly 2000 Au<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-734463-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-734463-1')">1</a></sup> in diameter which is overtaken by a biomass of tremendous proportions. Said biomass is a colonial organism with organic linkages that span the distances between celestial bodies and envelop the planets themselves, effectively turning the entire system into a breeding ground for smaller units of the organism, thus furthering its reach. A central mass which measures ~1.92 million km in diameter engulfs the system's sun, and a large, ovular maw sits atop it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Brace&nbsp;Yourself</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-You&nbsp;need&nbsp;more&nbsp;time&nbsp;to&nbsp;brace?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>[This maw ejects chitinous pods (SCP-XXXX-2) containing small, wormlike entities measuring 45&#160;cm in length (SCP-XXXX-2-A). These pods will crash within a 2&#160;km radius of the coordinates 84&quot;37'02&quot;S 68&quot;32'55&quot;E (Antarctica). Approximately one (1) hour after landing, these worms will &quot;hatch&quot; and burrow into the ice. It is shown that organisms proceed to grow at an indeterminate rate while in these conditions.</p>
<p>When exposed to a human being, SCP-XXXX-2-A will merge with the human's spinal column, controlling synapses and effectively taking the subject over. These instances are aggressive to all forms of life and show resistance to pain. Due to this outcome, a mobile task force (Hammer Down, maybe?) will be stationed within this two kilometer zone, and the trajectories of SCP-XXXX-2 will be tracked. Upon finding the crash zone, MTF will destroy SCP-XXXX-2 and SCP-XXXX-2-A by several means (I've written up a list of these means that will be in the official article.)</p>
<p>The final section of this SCP (I promise), referred to as SCP-XXXX-3, is a triangular portal with equa-distant sides that measures 15 meters tall, located at 84&quot;37'02&quot;S 68&quot;32'55&quot;E. It transports anyone entering to a corresponding portal within SCP-XXXX-1 (the solar system).<br />
]</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 and SCP-XXXX-3 were destroyed by MTF during an exploration, thus re-classifying SCP-XXXX as neutralized.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The article contains a few exploration logs, which culminates with an MTF force detonating a large device that cause the star to implode, eviscerating all components of the SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Several, the first of which will be the title and the &quot;<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Keter</span> Neutralized&quot; classification. An image too, if I can find one or make my own.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I was reading a bit about making first time Scips too complex/long. I fully intend to be as concise as possible (no 1730 here, folks). It might also be a bright idea for the struck-through class to be Keter-alterius, due to its alien origins.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
