			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845077">
									

<p>I think you've got an interesting concept on your hands, but I do feel like it could do with some refining.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="blockquote">
<p>Like why exactly is the crash site specifically within 2km of 84&quot;37'02&quot;S 68&quot;32'55&quot;E? Was it just luck that it wasn't in a more populated area? The size of the entity and the amount of biomass at it's disposal makes it seem slightly silly that its only a specific and small crash site without justified reasoning.</p>
<p>The portal seems a bit too 'Avengers 1' with an explosion through a portal into outer space, instantly neutralizing all elements of the skip. It feels like a obvious weak point of the entity that clearly has some form of higher or complex intelligence.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I do look forward to seeing the finished result and I do really like the mix of bodysnatchers, Lovecraft and The Thing going on!</p>

